      <h2>What does JPG compression mean?</h2>

      <p>
        JPG compression reduces the amount of data stored in an
        image file. This can help you save storage space, attach
        images to emails, and prepare pictures for websites.
        The amount of size reduction depends on the original image
        and the compression settings.
      </p>

      <h2>How to compress a JPG image with TinyShrink</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>Open the <a href="index.html">TinyShrink image compressor</a>.</li>
        <li>Select the JPG image you want to reduce. The current file limit is 20 MB.</li>
        <li>Choose JPG as the output format.</li>
        <li>Adjust the quality slider. Lower quality settings usually produce smaller files, but may reduce image detail.</li>
        <li>Compress the image and compare the original and compressed file sizes.</li>
        <li>Download the compressed image if you're happy with the result.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>How can I reduce JPG file size without losing too much quality?</h2>

      <p>
        Start with a moderate quality setting and compare the
        result with your original image. If the image still looks
        good, you can use the smaller version. For photographs,
        JPG is often a practical choice. Keep the original file
        when you need the best possible image quality.
      </p>

      <h2>Why should I compress images?</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Faster sharing:</strong> Smaller files are often easier to send.</li>
        <li><strong>Website performance:</strong> Smaller images can reduce page weight.</li>
        <li><strong>Storage savings:</strong> Compressed files can use less space.</li>
        <li><strong>Online forms:</strong> Compression may help meet file-size limits.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

