        No. TinyShrink processes images in your browser on your
        device. Your image file is not sent to our server for
        compression.
      </p>

      <h3>Can I compress PNG and WebP images too?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. TinyShrink supports JPG, PNG, and WebP images up to
        20 MB. Available output formats depend on the options in
        the compressor.
      </p>

      <h3>Will compression always make an image smaller?</h3>
      <p>
